{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27076984","formula":"C₂₄H₂₉N₃O₂","hill":"C24H29N3O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":24.0,"H":29.0,"N":3.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Daporinad"},"descriptions":{"en":"Daporinad (FK866, APO866), is a drug which acts as a selective inhibitor of the enzyme nicotinamide phosphoribosyltransferase (NAMPT). Levels of this enzyme are elevated in certain forms of cancer such as leukemia, and it was hoped that NAMPT inhibitors would be useful in the treatment of cancer. Unfortunately, dapinorad was unsuccessful in clinical trials due to lack of efficacy, but it still has antiinflammatory effects and may be useful for other medical applications such as arthritis, as well as being widely used as a tool compound for the study of NAMPT and its function."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":6914657,"mass":391.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CN(CCC1CCCCNC(=O)/C=C/C2=CN=CC=C2)C(=O)C3=CC=CC=C3","inchikey":"KPBNHDGDUADAGP-VAWYXSNFSA-N","iupac":"(E)-N-[4-(1-benzoylpiperidin-4-yl)butyl]-3-pyridin-3-ylprop-2-enamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6914657","atoms":58,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":6.057,"y":1.317,"z":2.189,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.73,"y":-2.908,"z":0.472,"el":"O"},{"x":4.143,"y":0.886,"z":0.917,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.097,"y":-2.106,"z":-0.977,"el":"N"},{"x":-7.474,"y":2.696,"z":-1.357,"el":"N"},{"x":1.58,"y":-0.463,"z":0.911,"el":"C"},{"x":2.596,"y":-0.647,"z":-0.228,"el":"C"},{"x":2.303,"y":-0.097,"z":2.218,"el":"C"},{"x":0.734,"y":-1.721,"z":1.093,"el":"C"},{"x":3.497,"y":0.578,"z":-0.365,"el":"C"},{"x":3.218,"y":1.111,"z":2.027,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.317,"y":-1.844,"z":-0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.183,"y":-3.087,"z":0.196,"el":"C"},{"x":5.518,"y":1.018,"z":1.125,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.21,"y":-3.236,"z":-0.92,"el":"C"},{"x":6.417,"y":0.772,"z":-0.009,"